    "text": "I labelled all 9 columns of job 1 and called `report_profile`.\n\n- **PHI:** `member_id`, `first_name`, `last_name`, `dob` and `patient_ref` are marked PHI. `member_id` is marked PHI because it links to a person outside the platform, which is what Rule 1 asks for.\n- **Not PHI:** `sex`, `plan_code`, `coverage_start` and `coverage_end`.\n\nFor the contract writer: `plan_code` has 8 rows with `GOLD`, which the contract does not allow (it allows HMO, PPO, EPO and HDHP). I labelled it as a code anyway, since that is a data issue for the drift review and not part of profiling.",
